
This is a fork of Lua 5.4.9, originally released on 10 Aug 2026.

This fork is binary incompatible with the original PUC-Rio Lua C API.

Its major modification is a change to the original setjmp/longjmp
based control flow. This version replaces it with an _Unwind ABI
exception runtime based control flow.

Beyond replacing setjmp/longjmp, this major modification allows
the Lua runtime to intercept any type of foreign runtime exception
Suppose a C++ function bound as a luaCFunction throws an exception,
the runtime will be able to intercept it, clean it and return with
a newly introduced LUA_ERREXCEPT error. The major improvement to
just compiling Lua in C++ is that the binding could be in Rust,
Ada or any other type of language and would still be able to
catch the exception. This enforces the protected calls as
safe barriers in both the Lua runtime but also the binary
interface of bindings.

Because this implementation is implemented in C only, it
relies on the personality attribute introduced in clang 23.
The LLVM toolchain version 23.1.0 released in 25 July 2026.

For installation instructions, license details, and
further information about Lua, see doc/readme.html.

